  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contributing to Improved Living Conditions and Safety for Flood Affected Populations in Pakistan through Provision of Multisectoral Assistance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">From June to October 2022, floods caused by heavy monsoon rains in Pakistan affected an estimated 33 million people, with an estimated 7.9 million persons temporarily displaced as of September 2022. Over 2 million houses have been affected, of which 805,000 have been fully destroyed. A considerable part of the displaced population has had to take shelter in relief camps set up by the government or in makeshift camps. The dire conditions and lack of services reported in these camps and displacement sites pose security threats to the affected populations. Sanitation conditions are poor, shelter recovery is crucial with receding flood waters, and the general protection environment is extremely dire with women and children at most risk. IOM is contributing to the delivery of lifesaving assistance to the affected populations while setting foundations for early recovery and durable solutions. Over a period of 12 months, IOM is providing multi-sectoral assistance to 33,703 households (235,924 individuals) in Balochistan, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa and Sindh provinces. IOM is providing emergency Shelter and Non-food Item (NFI) assistance; supporting Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) activities; increasing access to clean water, sanitation, hygiene and other basic services; and contributing to the provision of protection services.</narrative>
  </description>
